SUMMARY:Free Virtual History Lectures with the Diefenbunker: Canada's Cold War Museum
DESCRIPTION:We invite you to join virtually us this fall for the Diefenbunker Museum’s 5th annual Cold War Speaker Series! In this series of free events\, you will hear from experts sharing insights into Canada’s Cold War history. \nAll lectures are free to attend\, and open to all! Advance registration is required to receive the Zoom link and the recording after the event. \nThursday\, September 24\, at 7:00 p.m. ET  \nAllied Intelligence Networks in the Early Cold War \nDr. Timothy Andrews Sayle\, Associate Professor of History at the University of Toronto\, will share themes from his latest publication\, including recently declassified documents that explore the development of the allied indications network during the Cold War. \n 
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/free-virtual-history-lectures-with-the-diefenbunker-canadas-cold-war-museum-2/
LOCATION:online
GEO:56.130366;-106.346771
END:VEVENT
